  "placement": {
    "_band_comment": "Placement is a distance band around the hero, regardless of the camera (owner, 2026-09-15): the same request lands the same way at 16:9, 21:9, or with the view anywhere. The strict rung (FAR) takes a point between `far_min_distance` and `far_max_distance` from the hero -- 700 sits just past the 16:9 half-diagonal of 612 world px plus the old 96 px pad, so a 16:9 player still sees nothing appear, while a wider view may see an arrival at its edge; 1100 keeps the walk short. The middle rung (NEAR: a pack whose debt has aged past `relax_after`, or the strict rung empty) drops the ceiling and keeps `near_min_distance` as the keep-away.",
    "_starved_comment": "The last rung of the relaxation ladder, used only when no point passes the stricter rules -- which is what a player who camps on one island produces: its handful of points are all either on cooldown or inside the keep-away, and every pack becomes debt. At this rung the point cooldown shortens, so the same few points can be reused, and `starved_min_distance` is the only keep-away, so an enemy arrives at the edge of the screen rather than in the hero's lap; candidates here are also weighted by distance, which biases the draw outward.",
    "cooldown": 3.0,
    "far_min_distance": 700,
    "far_max_distance": 1100,
    "near_min_distance": 480,
    "relax_after": 5.0,
    "starved_min_distance": 420,
    "starved_cooldown": 0.5,
